%% Figure 4.12 – State Machine Diagram: payment_instruction.status (refund, disbursement, payout) · v3.2 · 05/11/2026 · Register v1.4
%% Same content as CrabShare_State_Machines.drawio, page "payment_instruction.status" (generated by gen-state.js, do not edit by hand).
%% «planned» = Register v1.4, not in code (class planned, grey dashed) · (not written by code) = CHECK value never written (class notwritten, orange dashed).
%% Labels are short (trigger [guard] / effect); the full label of each transition is in the %% line under it.
%% Design decisions of 05/11/2026 applied here were confirmed by the lead.
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Sent (not written by code)" as Sent
  state "Disputed (not written by code)" as Disputed
  [*] --> Created : / create instruction · UC18, UC39
  %% / created by a refund, a tranche release or a settlement approval · UC18, UC39 «planned» Refund of customer deposits when the batch does not open, and of a negative delivery balance
  Created --> Succeeded : send [account Open] / accepted · UC40
  %% send (Admin) [batch account Open, payee resolved] / gateway accepted: provider_transaction Out, sent_at, completed_at · UC40
  Created --> Failed : send / rejected · UC40
  %% send (Admin) / gateway rejected, sent_at · UC40
  Failed --> Succeeded : resend / accepted · UC40
  %% resend (Admin) / same reference CHI{id} · UC40
  Failed --> Failed : resend / rejected · UC40
  %% resend (Admin) / rejected again · UC40
  Created --> Sent : send [async provider] (not written by code)
  %% send (Admin) [asynchronous provider] / sent_at, wait for the callback (not written by code)
  Sent --> Succeeded : callback [done] (not written by code)
  %% provider callback [done] / completed_at (not written by code)
  Sent --> Failed : callback [failed] (not written by code)
  %% provider callback [failed] (not written by code)
  Succeeded --> Disputed : dispute notice (not written by code)
  %% dispute notice (provider) (not written by code)
  Disputed --> Succeeded : dispute closed (not written by code)
  %% dispute closed (provider) (not written by code)
  Succeeded --> [*]
  note right of Sent
    Sent - CHECK value (not written by code)
  end note
  note right of Disputed
    Disputed - CHECK value (not written by code)
  end note
  note right of Created
    «planned» on start → Created - Refund of customer deposits when the batch does not open, and of a negative delivery balance
  end note
  %% Created by a refund, a tranche release or a settlement approval only if: type Refund, Disbursement, Payout or TaxPayment; amount > 0 (UC18, UC39).
  %% The sandbox gateway answers synchronously: code goes Created → Succeeded or Failed and only sets sent_at. Sent and Disputed are allowed by the CHECK but never written (a known gap).
  %% On Succeeded: a Refund of a cancelled batch's contribution sets it Refunded; the last investor Payout closes the settlement and the batch (SettlementClosing.CloseIfPaidAsync); an order refund changes only the instruction.
  classDef planned stroke-dasharray:5 5,stroke:#64748b,color:#64748b,fill:#f8fafc
  classDef notwritten stroke-dasharray:5 5,stroke:#9a3412,fill:#f1f5f9
  classDef terminal fill:#f1f5f9,stroke:#64748b
  class Sent, Disputed notwritten
  class Succeeded terminal
